b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING incremental;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks, recursive procedures and function designators with value parameters (4.7, 5.4), the for statement (4.6) and conditional statements and expressions (3.3, 4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), sequences as parallel arrays of heads and tail indices for a sequence that is built up (systems file, Values), the message loop and observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8), and the holding of each relation until its places are known, written for this problem (METRICS.md, rule 19), with no period source;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: L e1 ... eL, the length and then the elements of the known sequence a of conc(a, s, t). A line 2: L e1 ... eL, the length and then the elements of the sequence of s = b. Elements are integers, an atom being its integer code;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P01b. Unknowns s and t, sequences. Stage 1: conc(a, s, t). Stage 2: s = b. A sequence is a cell index into the arrays hd and tl, 0 being the empty sequence, and a cell c being the sequence hd[c] followed by the sequence tl[c]. The cells are kept in arrays of a fixed size, cells, since a stage's sequence is read only when its stage is posed. Each unknown is a Boolean that says whether it has a value and the sequence it holds. Each relation is held as posed until enough of its places are known;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ cells;
  cells := 1000;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, len, top, a1, b2, sv, tv, held, pass, conc1, conc2;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ sk, tk, r1, r2, changed, inconsistent;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ hd, tl[1:cells];

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ cons(h, t);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ h, t; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ h, t;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a new cell, the sequence h followed by the sequence t;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ top := top + 1; hd[top] := h; tl[top] := t; cons := top e̲n̲d̲ cons;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ readseq(len);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ len; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ len;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a sequence of len elements, read from the input in order;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j, e, first, last, c;
    first := last := 0;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ len d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      e := read; c := cons(e, 0);
      i̲f̲ last = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ first := c e̲l̲s̲e̲ tl[last] := c;
      last := c
    e̲n̲d̲;
    readseq := first
  e̲n̲d̲ readseq;

  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ same(p, q);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ p, q; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p, q;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the equality of two sequences;
  same := i̲f̲ p = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ q = 0 e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ q = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ hd[p] = hd[q] t̲h̲e̲n̲ same(tl[p], tl[q]) e̲l̲s̲e̲ f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ conc(a, b);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ a, b; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a, b;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ conc(a, b, c), computing c from a and b by its cases, in order. Case 1: conc(the empty sequence, b, b). Case 2: conc(h followed by a, b, h followed by c) if conc(a, b, c);
  i̲f̲ a = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ conc1 := conc1 + 1; conc := b e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ c;
    conc2 := conc2 + 1;
    c := conc(tl[a], b);
    conc := cons(hd[a], c)
  e̲n̲d̲ conc;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine1;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of conc(a1, s, t): with s known, t is computed from a1 and s, or tested if known too. With s unknown it waits;
  i̲f̲ sk t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ c;
    c := conc(a1, sv);
    i̲f̲ tk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ ¬same(c, tv) t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ tv := c; tk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    r1 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲n̲d̲ examine1;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine2;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of s = b2: s is tested if known, else given b2;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲f̲ sk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ ¬same(sv, b2) t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ sv := b2; sk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    r2 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲n̲d̲ examine2;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ propagate;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ every held relation is examined, in the order posed, again and again until a whole pass gives no unknown a value;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲;
    f̲o̲r̲ pass := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ changed d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      changed := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
      i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine1;
      i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine2
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ propagate;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printseq(p);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ p; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a sequence, its elements in parentheses, separated by commas;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
    PRINTTEXT(`(');
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ p ≠ 0 d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ print(hd[p]); p := tl[p]; i̲f̲ p ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ') e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`)')
  e̲n̲d̲ printseq;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ relations;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: the relations held, with the values known put in their places;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      PRINTTEXT(`conc('); printseq(a1); PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      i̲f̲ sk t̲h̲e̲n̲ printseq(sv) e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`s');
      PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      i̲f̲ tk t̲h̲e̲n̲ printseq(tv) e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`t');
      PRINTTEXT(`)')
    e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ r1 ∧ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
    i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`s = '); printseq(b2) e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ relations;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  sk := tk := r1 := r2 := inconsistent := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
  top := conc1 := conc2 := 0;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: one message, the stage it poses, and then that stage's constants;
    code := read; k := read;
    i̲f̲ k = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ len := read; a1 := readseq(len); r1 := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ len := read; b2 := readseq(len); r2 := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;

    propagate;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answer: every unknown, and the relations still held;
    i̲f̲ ¬inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      PRINTTEXT(`[answer]s');
      i̲f̲ sk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` = '); printseq(sv) e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ r1 ∨ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` held') e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(` free');
      PRINTTEXT(`, t');
      i̲f̲ tk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` = '); printseq(tv) e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` held') e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(` free');
      i̲f̲ r1 ∨ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, where '); relations e̲n̲d̲;
      PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR
    e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the relations held, the values known, how many relations wait, and the applications of each case of conc;
    held := (i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0) + (i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0);
    PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
    i̲f̲ inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`held relations: ');
    i̲f̲ held = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`none') e̲l̲s̲e̲ relations;
    NLCR;
    i̲f̲ sk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind s]'); printseq(sv); PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ tk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind t]'); printseq(tv); PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ held > 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[suspended held-relations '); print(held); PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations conc/1 '); print(conc1); PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations conc/2 '); print(conc2); PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR;
    PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]')
  e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
